			<div class="content" id="post-content-4815809">
									

<p>Very tentative upvote. It's executed well enough for my tastes, but there are some glaring issues in here that I'd like to point out:</p>
<ul>
<li>SCP-5366 is described as a worldwide phenomenon with a variety of different effects; yet, the only case described is that of a singular GOC agent. The jump from the Description to the rest of the article is very jarring. If SCP-5366 was just &quot;the body of Agent Lynas&quot;, it would feel much cleaner as a whole.</li>
<li>The leading line &quot;SCP-5366 has been placed under the study of the Department of Theology and the Department of Science&quot; serves no overall purpose and could be safely axed.</li>
<li>&quot;Agent Lynas' repeated phrase has been included per Foundation record keeping policy&quot; I don't see what's added by saying that it's only included because of &quot;record keeping policy&quot;.</li>
<li>The dialogue feels very one-sided. I know that's the point, but it makes me wonder if allowing Lynas to hear Peri would make the SCP stronger.</li>
</ul>
<p>Like I said above, the unsettling execution (even if it gets a bit too close to <a href="/scp-2718">SCP-2718</a> for my liking at points) wins my upvote, but these issues distracted me from that somewhat.</p>

							</div>

								
					
